IMPORT prelude

-- Ngee Ann Kongsi (Incorporation) Ordinance 1933 (Singapore) -- who may join the Kongsi (s 3(2), (4), First Schedule), who may sit on
-- and be expelled from its Committee of Management (s 7(11), (13)), who may be President (s 9(2), (4)), the Committee quorum (s 10(1)),
-- requisitioning an extraordinary general meeting (s 13), notice of and quorum at general meetings (ss 14(2), 16(1), (1A)), dealings in
-- the Kongsi's land (s 20(1), (6)), and the compulsory 75% of net income given away and the ring-fencing of sale proceeds (s 20A(1)-(3)).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation (version in force from 1 April 2022), as deposited at
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/NAKIO1933.txt. The revised edition "incorporates all amendments up to and including 1 December 2021";
-- the latest amendment annotated in the body is Act 25 of 2021 wef 01/04/2022 (s 20(1), (2)).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Requirement REQ-0240 in subjects/sg/requirements.jsonl: tier 4 of the remaining Singapore Acts, ordered by everyday-life
-- relevance. It asks what the Ordinance decides for a person or business it applies to; no scenario has asked a sharper question yet.
-- SCOPED to the rules a Teochew applicant, a member, a Committee member, a buyer or lessee of Kongsi land, or a beneficiary of its
-- donations would meet. Not encoded: the recitals and the first Committee (s 8), ex-officio membership (s 7(2)-(5A)), retirement
-- rotation and the lunar-calendar dates (ss 7(6)-(7), 11(2), 12(1)), casual vacancies (s 7(9), (10)), Honorary Past Presidents
-- (s 9A), Gazette publication (s 9B), accounts (s 11), records and the seal (ss 17, 18), vesting (s 19 and Second Schedule), the
-- court procedure (s 20(2)-(5)), bank-account rules and Ministerial powers (s 20A(4)-(7)), subsidiaries (s 20B) and rules (s 21).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text, following the conventions of the finished naive rows (the writing-l4-rules
-- skill was not available in this session). No pipeline, no coverage table, no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Ngee Ann Kongsi (Incorporation) Ordinance 1933`

§§ `3(2) and First Schedule -- who may be elected a member`

-- s 3(2): "No person shall be eligible for membership of the Corporation unless at the time of his application for membership --
-- (a) he has attained the age of 21 years and has ordinarily resided in Singapore for not less than 2 years and is a member of the
-- Teochew Community of or originating from one of the said Eight Districts; and (b) he fills up and signs a declaration in the form
-- set forth in the First Schedule."
-- s 3(1): even an eligible applicant is elected only if the Committee "in its absolute discretion" considers it desirable; s 3(3): it
-- "may, but shall not be bound to," give reasons for a rejection. Eligibility is therefore necessary, never sufficient.
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `years ordinarily resident in Singapore` IS A NUMBER
    `Teochew of one of the Eight Districts` IS A BOOLEAN
    `signed the First Schedule declaration` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the applicant` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the applicant is eligible for membership` IF
        `the applicant`'s `age` AT LEAST 21
    AND `the applicant`'s `years ordinarily resident in Singapore` AT LEAST 2
    AND `the applicant`'s `Teochew of one of the Eight Districts`
    AND `the applicant`'s `signed the First Schedule declaration`

-- First Schedule: the applicant declares himself "being a non-Christian and a member of the Teochew Community of Singapore from the
-- (c) [District]". Section 3(2)(a) says nothing of religion; the bar on Christians comes only through the words of the declaration.
-- INFERENCE (not stated in the text): a Christian cannot truthfully make the declaration and so cannot satisfy s 3(2)(b).
GIVEN `non-Christian` IS A BOOLEAN, `Teochew from a District` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the declaration can be made truthfully` IF
    `non-Christian` AND `Teochew from a District`

§§ `3(4) -- applying again after rejection`

-- s 3(4): a rejected applicant is not "entitled again to apply for membership of the Corporation until the expiration of 6 months
-- from the date of his previous application." (Measured from the APPLICATION, not the rejection.)
GIVEN `months since the previous application` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a rejected applicant may apply again` IF
    `months since the previous application` AT LEAST 6

§§ `7(11) -- who may be elected to the Committee of Management`

-- s 7(11): "No person shall be eligible for election as a member of the Committee of Management unless -- (a) he shall have attained
-- the age of 22 years and is a person professing the religions (other than the Christian religion) professed by members or some of
-- the members in Singapore of the Teochew Community of the said Eight Districts; (b) he shall have been a member of the Corporation
-- for at least 6 months prior to the date of the annual general meeting ... or other date at which his election is proposed."
DECLARE Candidate HAS
    `age` IS A NUMBER
    `professes the Teochew religions other than Christianity` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months a member before the election date` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is eligible for election to the Committee` IF
        `the candidate`'s `age` AT LEAST 22
    AND `the candidate`'s `professes the Teochew religions other than Christianity`
    AND `the candidate`'s `months a member before the election date` AT LEAST 6

§§ `7(13) -- expulsion from the Committee`

-- s 7(13): a member who misconducts himself or is unfit "may, by the vote of two-thirds of the members of the Committee of Management
-- attending at a meeting specially called to consider the matter, be expelled ... but he shall at the said meeting be given an
-- opportunity of explaining his conduct ... and no vote shall be passed at such meeting unless such opportunity aforesaid shall have
-- been given." (Two-thirds of those ATTENDING, not of the whole Committee.)
GIVEN `votes for expulsion` IS A NUMBER, `members attending` IS A NUMBER, `opportunity to explain given` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the expulsion is validly voted` IF
        `opportunity to explain given`
    AND `votes for expulsion` TIMES 3 AT LEAST `members attending` TIMES 2

§§ `9(1), (2), (4) -- who may be President`

-- s 9(1): the Committee elects "from their number a President, 2 Vice-Presidents, an Honorary Secretary and an Honorary Treasurer".
-- s 9(2): "No person shall be elected or appointed to be an officer of the Corporation unless he shall have attained the age of 25
-- years." s 9(4): "Any person elected to be the President or Honorary Treasurer of the Corporation for 2 years shall not be entitled
-- to hold office as such for the next ensuing 2 years."
GIVEN `age` IS A NUMBER, `on the Committee` IS A BOOLEAN, `was President for the 2 years just ended` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be elected President` IF
        `age` AT LEAST 25
    AND `on the Committee`
    AND (NOT `was President for the 2 years just ended`)

§§ `10(1) -- Committee quorum`

-- s 10(1): the Committee "shall meet together at least once in every 3 months ... and 7 members shall form a quorum."
GIVEN `Committee members present` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee meeting is quorate` IF
    `Committee members present` AT LEAST 7

§§ `13 -- requisitioning an extraordinary general meeting`

-- s 13(1): "Upon receipt of a requisition by at least 5 members of the Committee of Management or by at least 10 members of the
-- Corporation the Committee of Management shall proceed to convene an extraordinary general meeting". (2): the requisition "shall
-- state the objects of the meeting and shall be signed by the requisitionists and deposited at the office of the Corporation".
-- The two thresholds are alternatives; the text gives no way of adding Committee signatories to ordinary members.
GIVEN `Committee signatories` IS A NUMBER, `member signatories` IS A NUMBER, `states objects and is deposited at the office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Committee must convene an extraordinary general meeting` IF
        `states objects and is deposited at the office`
    AND (   `Committee signatories` AT LEAST 5
         OR `member signatories` AT LEAST 10)

-- s 13(3): acknowledgment within 10 days of receipt, and the meeting held "within 20 days from the receipt". (4): if the Committee
-- does not do so "the requisitionists or a majority of them may themselves convene the meeting".
GIVEN `days since the requisition was received` IS A NUMBER, `meeting already held` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the requisitionists may convene the meeting themselves` IF
        `days since the requisition was received` GREATER THAN 20
    AND (NOT `meeting already held`)

§§ `14(2), (4) -- notice of a general meeting`

-- s 14(2): written notice of every general meeting "not less than 7 clear days before the day on which the general meeting is to be
-- held". (4): a posted notice is "deemed to be served at the time when the notice would, in the ordinary course of post, be
-- delivered". INFERENCE: "clear days" excludes both the day of service and the day of the meeting, so the days strictly between them
-- are counted: a notice deemed served on day 0 is in time for a meeting on day 8 or later.
GIVEN `days from deemed service to the meeting` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the notice is in time` IF
    `days from deemed service to the meeting` MINUS 1 AT LEAST 7

§§ `16(1), (1A) -- quorum at a general meeting`

-- s 16(1): "Subject to subsection (1A), 20 members of the Corporation shall form a quorum at any general meeting." (1A): "If, after
-- 30 minutes from the time appointed for a general meeting, there are fewer than 20 members ... present ..., any 10 or more members
-- of the Corporation present at that place shall form a quorum". INFERENCE: "after 30 minutes" read as once 30 minutes have passed.
GIVEN `members present` IS A NUMBER, `minutes after the appointed time` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the general meeting is quorate` IF
        `members present` AT LEAST 20
    OR  (`minutes after the appointed time` AT LEAST 30 AND `members present` AT LEAST 10)

§§ `20(1), (6) -- dealing in the Kongsi's land`

-- s 20(1): the Corporation "shall not sell, exchange, mortgage, lease (otherwise than upon a tenancy not exceeding 3 years) or
-- otherwise alienate or encumber any immovable property ... without the permission of the General Division of the High Court, and
-- ... shall not purchase any immovable property out of the funds of the Corporation without such permission, and no application ...
-- shall be made without a resolution being first passed at a general meeting of members held for such purpose."
DECLARE Dealing IS ONE OF
    `a sale`
    `an exchange`
    `a mortgage`
    `a lease`
    `a purchase out of the Corporation's funds`
    `accepting a gift of land`

GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `lease term in months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the dealing needs the High Court's permission` IF
    CONSIDER `the dealing`
    WHEN `a lease` THEN `lease term in months` GREATER THAN 36
    WHEN `accepting a gift of land` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 20(6): "Any immovable property so sold, exchanged, leased or otherwise alienated, except by way of mortgage, shall be held by the
-- purchaser or person exchanging or otherwise taking the same free from the trusts imposed under this Ordinance." ("So" -- i.e. with
-- the court's decree under s 20(4).)
GIVEN `the dealing` IS A Dealing, `made under a High Court decree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the taker holds free of the Ordinance's trusts` IF
        `made under a High Court decree`
    AND CONSIDER `the dealing`
        WHEN `a sale` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `an exchange` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `a lease` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `20A(1), (2) -- 75% of net income given away`

-- s 20A(2): net income is "A − B þ C" in the deposit; the "þ" is a mis-rendered plus sign (INFERENCE from the definitions: C is
-- unspent sale proceeds of the preceding period, which can only be meant to be added back). A is income other than from selling
-- relevant assets or land or withdrawing relevant deposits; B is operating expenses reasonably incurred plus depreciation of fixed
-- assets; C is the preceding period's sale and withdrawal proceeds not reinvested by the end of this period.
GIVEN `A income` IS A NUMBER, `B expenses and depreciation` IS A NUMBER, `C unreinvested proceeds` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the net income` MEANS `A income` MINUS `B expenses and depreciation` PLUS `C unreinvested proceeds`

-- s 20A(1): the Committee "shall, in each accounting period ..., set apart 75% of the net income ... and shall, by the end of the
-- next accounting period, donate -- (a) 25% of the net income to the Ngee Ann Polytechnic ...; (b) 40% of the net income to such
-- other educational institutions and in such manner as the Minister may approve; and (c) 10% of the net income to other charitable
-- purposes in Singapore."
GIVEN `net` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the donation to Ngee Ann Polytechnic` MEANS `net` TIMES 25 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `net` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the donation to Minister-approved educational institutions` MEANS `net` TIMES 40 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `net` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the donation to other charitable purposes` MEANS `net` TIMES 10 DIVIDED BY 100

GIVEN `net` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the amount set apart` MEANS
        `the donation to Ngee Ann Polytechnic` `net`
    PLUS `the donation to Minister-approved educational institutions` `net`
    PLUS `the donation to other charitable purposes` `net`

§§ `20A(3), (5) -- what sale proceeds may be spent on`

-- s 20A(3): "Subject to subsections (1) and (2), no moneys received by the Corporation ... from -- (a) the sale, disposition or
-- compulsory acquisition of any relevant asset or immovable property ...; or (b) the withdrawal of any relevant deposit ... shall be
-- utilised otherwise than for the purchase of any relevant asset or immovable property, or the making of any relevant deposit".
-- (5): other moneys in a relevant bank account may also go to operating expenses reasonably incurred, the s 20A(1) donations, and
-- donations "for any purpose consistent with the objects and general purposes of the Corporation referred to in section 6".
-- (The route by which unreinvested proceeds re-enter net income as C, and so 75% of them are donated, is not modelled here.)
DECLARE Use IS ONE OF
    `buying an investment asset`
    `buying land`
    `making an investment deposit with a licensed bank`
    `paying operating expenses`
    `a donation within the section 6 objects`
    `a purpose outside the section 6 objects`

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `sale proceeds may be applied to the use` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `buying an investment asset` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `buying land` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `making an investment deposit with a licensed bank` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the use` IS A Use
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `other banked moneys may be applied to the use` IF
    CONSIDER `the use`
    WHEN `a purpose outside the section 6 objects` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
